{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 23, :comments ["<b>You shall ascend.</b> Ben Zuta said: it is in the construct state from the root מעל. But he did not open his eyes to see, for mem is a root letter in מעל, as proven by ומעלה בו מעל (Numbers 5:12). And behold, מעל is in the pattern of נעל, in the plural non-construct: נעלות בלות ומטולאות (Joshua 9:5). And behold, it ought to have a chirik under the bet and a kamatz under the ayin in בִמְעָלות, except that its meaning is like ומעלות שבעה עלותיו (Ezekiel 40:26). Now Ben Zuta thought to ascend the ladder of wisdom with his vanities, and his nakedness was exposed upon him. And so they call every heretic who does not believe the words of our ancients by this name. And this is the commandment of ramps, encompassing every earthen altar, of stones or of copper — every altar made for the Name, as it is written מזבחי."], :book :exodus, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 20, :notes {0 "The pun in 'ascend the ladder' plays on תעלה ('you shall ascend') and מעלות ('ramps'); both preserved. 'כאשר הוא כתוב מזבחי' likely cites the phrase 'מזבחי אדמה' from the same verse, left untranslated as it functions as a scriptural citation."}, :source-witnesses [["Piotrkow, 1907-1911" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH990020973480205171/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:36:35.940150524Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}